{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/989370-upper-limit-for-first-change","id":989370,"title":"Upper Limit for First Change?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-18T08:55:53-07:00","id":989370,"title":"Upper Limit for First Change?","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> I had been reading into making a Werewolf character as of late. The books indicated that the First Change typically happens around adolescence. However, that it can also occur to those a little older than that as well. Is there any upper limit on the age when someone might undergo their First Change or can it essentially still occur at any point in one's life? Apologies if I missed any obvious information on it elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T09:27:15-07:00","id":989388,"title":"","content":"There is technically neither an upper nor a lower limit. Gaia does what Gaia does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T09:30:03-07:00","id":989390,"title":"","content":"It can happen at any time although generally most Lost Cubs will change when they are quite young still (twenties or thirties). The Black Furies Tribebook revised had one of their example characters have their first change as a grandmother in her fifties. That would be rare though.<br /> <br /> There are Garou who NEVER have their first change, and they typically have severe mental problems as they have buried the wolf too deep in their psyche. They are known as Lunatics, and they are the counterparts of the typical cinematic cursed lycanthrope. They were more prominent in first edition, but later editions downplayed them.<br /> <br /> I would say these are typically homid only problems. I don't think metis or lupus Garou have any real delays when they change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T09:35:06-07:00","id":989396,"title":"","content":"I seem to remember a Shadowlord (Carlson Ruah?) written up in Warriors oif Rage that changed at 26 and it said he was an extremely late changer. By that point in his life he had given up any expectations of going through the change. Until hearing about the grandmother example above, that was the oldest canon First Change I was aware of.<br /> Mind you, it's worth stating that different editions have changes things so there isn't a certain age limit by any means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T10:00:02-07:00","id":989413,"title":"","content":"I appreciate the information. Glad to find I wasn't way off track with what I had seen. As far as rare and has issues.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are Garou who NEVER have their first change, and they typically have severe mental problems as they have buried the wolf too deep in their psyche. </div> </div> </div>I heard mental problems were sometimes related to repression. Do you think playing an unchanged character late in life would be possible, or would the related impairments be too significant? It was either in a tribe book or auspice book where I saw mention of that sort of thing, but it didn't seem to relate how severe these derangements might be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T16:49:25-07:00","id":989614,"title":"","content":"That's up to you and what you want, I think. The Lunatics weren't thought of as PCs, but neither were develped that much, so I guess you can make one with whatever Drangements you and your ST think appropriate. They are a rare and variable phenomenom, so it isn't unbelievable to have one stable enough to be playable, or even a rare one that's almost sane. The bottom line is the trauma of the Garou instincts assaulting someone who deny it enough to stop it happening.<br /> <br /> Oh, and this poor soul can also be a late Change, so the traumatic experience occurs already on an old and maybe more mentally tough person. It isn't very likely, but certainly not impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T18:08:10-07:00","id":989639,"title":"","content":"I think that Delayed Change would be an interesting Merit for one of the Kinfolk to possess. I think that I would give it a price of 6 BP (3 BP if the Kinfolk possesses one permanent Derangement related to the delayed change, 1 BP if the Kinfolk possesses two permanent Derangements related to the delayed change, and 0 BP if the Kinfolk possesses three permanent Derangements related to the delayed change). When the Kinfolk experiences the First Change, the Derangements would become temporary, allowing them to be healed over time, and they would gain +1/+1/+0 Attribute points and +2/+2/+1 Ability points, +3 permanent Renown, Rank 1, an Auspice, a Breed, a Tribe, and three Gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T18:13:57-07:00","id":989642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/989370-upper-limit-for-first-change?p=989639#post989639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that Delayed Change would be an interesting Merit for one of the Kinfolk to possess. I think that I would give it a price of 6 BP (3 BP if the Kinfolk possesses one permanent Derangement related to the delayed change, 1 BP if the Kinfolk possesses two permanent Derangements related to the delayed change, and 0 BP if the Kinfolk possesses three permanent Derangements related to the delayed change). When the Kinfolk experiences the First Change, the Derangements would become temporary, allowing them to be healed over time, and they would gain +1/+1/+0 Attribute points and +2/+2/+1 Ability points, +3 permanent Renown, Rank 1, an Auspice, a Breed, a Tribe, and three Gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem: delayed change Changers aren't Kin unless they're Ratkin or Corax (or Camazotz, in particular games). They're Changers. They should be created as such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T18:51:23-07:00","id":989654,"title":"","content":"Are you sure? I imagine that everyone who becomes Garou are Kinfolk before they change. Otherwise, they would have three Gifts before they would have Gnosis or Rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T19:00:01-07:00","id":989661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/989370-upper-limit-for-first-change?p=989654#post989654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you sure? I imagine that everyone who becomes Garou are Kinfolk before they change. Otherwise, they would have three Gifts before they would have Gnosis or Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why?<br /> Garou don't naturally have Gifts. You get them at character creation because you've been a Garou for some time (a few months to a couple of years depending on individual story). You've built up starting renown and gone through your Rite of Passage and have earned your 3 starting Gifts. They don't come free with your First Change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T20:46:56-07:00","id":989701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/989370-upper-limit-for-first-change?p=989654#post989654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you sure? I imagine that everyone who becomes Garou are Kinfolk before they change. Otherwise, they would have three Gifts before they would have Gnosis or Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that some part of KABA mentioned pre-change Garou and Fera being assumed to have the minimum starting value by Breed and Auspice for their Rage and Gnosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T21:45:25-07:00","id":989716,"title":"","content":"So, how could anyone not notice a pre-change Ahroun? They would be a mortal with Rage 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T03:20:16-07:00","id":989812,"title":"","content":"Because they don't have Frenzy or the ability to use Rage yet, just the numbers. The same for Gnosis, since you'll see that even Kin with Gnosis have few uses for this.<br /> <br /> And then you add that Delayed Changers almost always don't know of Changers at all, that's why they are Delayed Changers. They didn't had anyone who could help with those new instincts, so it is probable no one could recognise their Rage and Gnosis, either.<br /> <br /> Remember, whyle a Late Change is a natural, if rare, happenstance, a Delayed Change is anything but. It is an extreme repression caused by extreme circumstances.<br /> <br /> Indeed, most kinfolk advantages wouldn't do much for those people. They don't need Lunacy, as an example, to simply run with blind fear at the sight of a Garou, and to try to reason the encounter later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T08:04:10-07:00","id":989878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So, how could anyone not notice a pre-change Ahroun? They would be a mortal with Rage 5.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> With two or three exceptions, Garou and Fera don't count as mortal pre-change. Because they're born that way.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/989370-upper-limit-for-first-change?p=989812#post989812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because they don't have Frenzy or the ability to use Rage yet, just the numbers. The same for Gnosis, since you'll see that even Kin with Gnosis have few uses for this.<br /> <br /> And then you add that Delayed Changers almost always don't know of Changers at all, that's why they are Delayed Changers. They didn't had anyone who could help with those new instincts, so it is probable no one could recognise their Rage and Gnosis, either.<br /> <br /> Remember, whyle a Late Change is a natural, if rare, happenstance, a Delayed Change is anything but. It is an extreme repression caused by extreme circumstances.<br /> <br /> Indeed, most kinfolk advantages wouldn't do much for those people. They don't need <b>Lunacy</b>, as an example, to simply run with blind fear at the sight of a Garou, and to try to reason the encounter later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forsaken Slip? (^VVVVVV^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T14:58:51-07:00","id":990121,"title":"","content":"Quite indeed, I didn't had the time to verify the right term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T18:47:05-07:00","id":990199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/989370-upper-limit-for-first-change?p=989413#post989413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think playing an unchanged character late in life would be possible, or would the related impairments be too significant? It was either in a tribe book or auspice book where I saw mention of that sort of thing, but it didn't seem to relate how severe these derangements might be.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something to be worked out with your ST during character creation. In canon, there are people (Garou and kinfolk) who work with Lunatics so they can learn how to change (not all Lunatics are able to do so, and they remain in various states of mental illness). After they change, they seem to be OK as the wolf is released and therefore the character isn't fighting their instincts anymore. Whether there is any lasting psychological damage would be up to you and your ST.<br /> <br /> I had a character concept once where he was a Lost Cub and practically a &quot;Lunatic&quot; which he partially medicated by prescription drugs and psychotherapy. Once he actually changed (due to help by Garou who found him), he was fine.<br /> <br /> I think this is a perfectly acceptable background element to your character, but talk with your ST to see if he'd like any changes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T14:01:48-07:00","id":990619,"title":"","content":"I think it would be interesting to play a character that experienced the First Change when he was in his thirties or forties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T20:37:24-07:00","id":991243,"title":"","content":"I currently play a character who changed very early, at 12, and was almost a Lunatic, just didn't had the willpower to completely repress the Change. It was quite traumatic for her, and for some months she was almost as crazy as any Lunatic, believing she was a terrible monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}